# How to cite The Digital Historian's Toolbox. GitHub shows a "Cite this repository" button from
# this file, and Zenodo uses it to describe each archived release.
#
# BEFORE THE FIRST RELEASE: replace [EDITOR NAMES] with the editors (one "- family-names /
# given-names" block per person; add "orcid:" if you like) and check the other fields.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this catalogue, please cite the archived version of the data you used
  (each release has its own DOI on Zenodo).
type: dataset
title: "The Digital Historian’s Toolbox"
abstract: >-
  A curated, community-submitted catalogue of the software tools and public datasets
  historians use, with every entry linked to the projects that used it. Research uses
  are kept separate from corpus building and from evaluations (benchmarks), and AI tools
  carry "historian’s notes" on where sources go, how the tool has been tested, and how
  it fails on historical material.
authors:
  - name: "[EDITOR NAMES]"
repository-code: "https://github.com/polayj/digital-historians-toolbox"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - digital history
  - digital humanities
  - research tools
  - datasets
  - OCR
  - HTR
  - historical methods
